WEBVTT

00:00:00.061 --> 00:00:01.701
They taught a baby to fear.

00:00:01.711 --> 00:00:02.891
On purpose.

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:06.361
In 1920, John Watson and Rosalie Rayner

00:00:06.371 --> 00:00:09.019
showed an eleven-month-old a white rat.

00:00:09.029 --> 00:00:10.957
Each time he touched it, they struck

00:00:10.967 --> 00:00:13.018
a steel bar behind his back.

00:00:13.028 --> 00:00:14.768
Soon the rat alone seemed to frighten

00:00:14.778 --> 00:00:17.291
him, and other furry things too.

00:00:17.301 --> 00:00:18.986
His mother took him away.

00:00:19.049 --> 00:00:21.628
For decades, nobody knew who he was.

00:00:21.638 --> 00:00:25.703
In 2009, one team proposed
Douglas Merritte,

00:00:25.713 --> 00:00:27.906
who died of an illness at six.

00:00:27.916 --> 00:00:31.381
In 2014, a second team proposed another

00:00:31.391 --> 00:00:34.249
nurse's baby, recorded as Albert.

00:00:34.259 --> 00:00:37.359
His recorded weight closely
matched Little Albert's.

00:00:37.369 --> 00:00:40.141
If they're right, he
lived to eighty-seven.

00:00:40.154 --> 00:00:42.469
His niece recalled a mild dislike of

00:00:42.479 --> 00:00:44.731
dogs, which nobody can tie to the

00:00:44.741 --> 00:00:46.041
experiment.

00:00:46.054 --> 00:00:48.366
The teams still disagree.
